# Internal-only acceptance-test environment tooling. Kept in the internal repo
# but excluded from `git archive` output (release tarballs / export-based
# publishing) so it does not ship to the public provider repo.
#
# NOTE: `export-ignore` ONLY affects `git archive`. It does NOT prevent a plain
# `git merge`/push from carrying this directory into another repository. If the
# internal -> public sync is a git merge, additionally keep testenv/ off the
# branch that is merged to public (or strip it on the public side).
testenv/ export-ignore
testenv/** export-ignore
